# DIAGNOSTICS

The parser's errors, each with the line it refers to, are:

| Error | Cause |
| `unterminated quoted value` | a quoted value with no closing `"` on its line |
| `control character in a quoted value; use x"…"` | a control character inside quotes |
| `invalid UTF-8 in a quoted value` | the bytes inside quotes are not UTF-8 |
| `bad hex value` | a byte that is not a hexadecimal digit, or no closing `"` |
| `odd number of digits in a hex value` | half a byte |
| `control character in a key` | a control character in a key |
| `empty key` | a `=` or a `"` where a key should start |
| `invalid UTF-8 in a key` | a key that is not UTF-8 |
| `quote inside a bare value` | a `"` inside a value written bare |
| `control character in a value; use x"…"` | a control character in a bare value |
| `empty bare value; write ""` | `key=` with nothing after it |
| `invalid UTF-8 in a value; use x"…"` | a bare value that is not UTF-8 |
| `quote inside a key` | a `"` straight after a key |
| `junk after a value` | a quoted or hex value not followed by a space or the end of the line |
| `duplicate key` | a key twice in one record |
| `too many tuples in one record` | more than 128 |
| `indented line with no record above it` | the first line of tuples is indented |
| `record longer than 64 KiB` | too long |
| `scratch space exhausted` | the caller's buffer for decoded values is too small |

# BUGS

The writer does not refuse a duplicate key, a 129th tuple or a record longer than 64 KiB, so it can write a record the parser refuses, though `ndb.h` says nothing is written that would read back differently.

A record's length is measured to the end of the blank and comment lines that follow it, so trailing comments count against its 64 KiB.

A number's hexadecimal digits must be lower case, though a hex value's may be either.
